coder › Fixed in `src/range.ts` and added tests in `src/range.test.ts`, on branch `fix-range-overlaps`.

What changed:
- `overlaps` now uses strict `<` on both sides (`aStart < bEnd && bStart < aEnd`), so touching ranges with an exclusive end no longer overlap.
- Added a `parseBoundary` helper that throws `TypeError` (message includes the offending string) when `Date.parse` returns `NaN`.
- Added `RangeError` (message includes both values) when a range's end is before its start.
- Added a zero-length guard: if either range has `start === end`, it overlaps nothing, including itself.

Tests added:
- touching ranges do not overlap
- ranges starting at the same instant overlap
- zero-length range overlaps nothing, not even itself
- unparseable start throws `TypeError` naming the value
- unparseable end throws `TypeError` naming the value
- end before start throws `RangeError`

